Dataset Description
This file contains a synthetic order instance for experimental evaluation in an AP-related delivery scenario:

Expr1_order_instance_for_AP_(11_12)_orderNum_10_stationNum_3_lockerNum_1051_droneNum_20_seed_1.csv

The dataset records a set of delivery orders, where each row represents one order request with its origin and destination information. Specifically, it includes the identifiers of the merchant (store_id) and customer (home_id), together with their corresponding geographic coordinates.

This instance can be used in studies on drone delivery, parcel locker assignment, order dispatching, route planning, and other last-mile logistics optimization problems.

File Naming Convention
The file name encodes the experimental configuration:

Expr1_order_instance_for_AP_(11_12)_orderNum_10_stationNum_3_lockerNum_1051_droneNum_20_seed_1.csv

The components can be interpreted as follows:

Expr1: experiment ID or experiment group
order_instance_for_AP: order instance generated for the AP scenario
(11_12): scenario identifier, region index, or parameter setting label
orderNum_10: number of orders = 10
stationNum_3: number of stations = 3
lockerNum_1051: number of lockers = 1051
droneNum_20: number of drones = 20
seed_1: random seed used for instance generation = 1
Note: The exact meaning of AP and (11_12) should be defined according to the corresponding project or experiment setup.

File Format
The file is stored in CSV format. The first row is the header:

<CSV>
order_ID,store_id,home_id,org_lng,org_lat,des_lng,des_lat
Attribute Description
Column Name	Type	Description
order_ID	float / integer-like	Order identifier
store_id	float / integer-like	Identifier of the origin store (merchant)
home_id	float / integer-like	Identifier of the destination customer/home
org_lng	float	Longitude of the order origin
org_lat	float	Latitude of the order origin
des_lng	float	Longitude of the order destination
des_lat	float	Latitude of the order destination
