Semantic Meaning of Each Record
Each row in the dataset corresponds to one delivery order:

the order originates from a merchant represented by store_id;
the delivery destination is a customer/home represented by home_id;
org_lng and org_lat specify the geographic coordinates of the merchant;
des_lng and des_lat specify the geographic coordinates of the customer/home.
These records can be directly used as input for optimization models or simulation frameworks involving origin-destination order demand.

Data Characteristics
According to the file name, this instance contains the following configuration:

Number of orders: 10
Number of stations: 3
Number of lockers: 1051
Number of drones: 20
Random seed: 1
Notes and Data Usage Considerations
1. Identifier Format
Although order_ID, store_id, and home_id appear as floating-point values in the CSV file, they should be interpreted as categorical or integer identifiers in most applications.

It is recommended to cast them to integer type after loading the file.

2. Order ID Uniqueness
In the provided sample, all values in order_ID are 0.0. This may indicate one of the following:

the order identifier field was not uniquely assigned during data generation; or
this field is not used in the current experimental setting.
If unique order indexing is required, users are advised to regenerate or relabel the order IDs.

3. Geographic Coordinates
The coordinate fields are represented in decimal degrees. Before performing distance calculation, map matching, or routing operations, please verify that the coordinate reference system is consistent with the geographic tools or map services being used.

4. Reproducibility
The suffix seed_1 indicates that this instance was generated using random seed 1. To reproduce the same dataset, the same generation parameters and seed value should be used.

Recommended Loading Method
Python Example
<PYTHON>
import pandas as pd
file_path = "Expr1_order_instance_for_AP_(11_12)_orderNum_10_stationNum_3_lockerNum_1051_droneNum_20_seed_1.csv"
df = pd.read_csv(file_path)
# Convert identifier columns to integers if needed
df["order_ID"] = df["order_ID"].astype(int)
df["store_id"] = df["store_id"].astype(int)
df["home_id"] = df["home_id"].astype(int)
print(df.head())
print("Number of records:", len(df))
